  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal, by reason of loss of houses -although in despair- which complements with the original estate and integral to the character and appearance of the area, with no evidence to suggest cannot be refurbished would be harmful to the heritage and not promote sustainability; also the proposal, by reason of its position, size, design and external appearance, including basements and terraces, would be an intrusive development, out of scale and character with the prevailing pattern of development, a loss of privacy to neighbours and have a serious and adverse effect on the visual amenity of the locality and the wider Gunnersbury Park Conservation Area (Article 4), contrary to Gunnersbury Park Conservation Area Appraisal, Local Plan policies SC7, CC1, CC2 and CC4 and London Plan Policies D4, HC1 and the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal would result in an intensification of the use of the site leading to an increase in noise and disturbance in the area, and no measures are proposed to mitigate the harm, would cause a serious and adverse effect on the amenity enjoyed by occupants of neighbouring properties and the character of the area, contrary to Local Plan Policies SC7 and CC2 and the National Planning Policy Framework",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal provides inadequate quality of accommodation; due to poor outlook and light levels and provision of insufficient private and communal amenity spaces, and provision of basement accommodation would be detrimental to the amenities enjoyed by prospective occupants of this development, contrary to Local Plan policies SC5, CC2, and London Plan Policy D6, London Plan Housing SPG and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposal by reason of, insufficient cycle parking spaces and poor waste and recycling arrangement, lack of delivery and servicing information would result in adverse impacts to the transport network, active transport mode promotion and waste and recycling collection, contrary to London Plan Policy T5, T6, T7, Local Plan Policy EC2, EQ7 and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework.   ",
    "Reason : 5 - The submitted biodiversity information does not meet the requirements, due to loss of landscaping and failure to provide high quality replacement and would harm the natural environment and biodiversity of the site and wider area, contrary to Schedule 7A of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, London Plan Policy G6, Local Plan Policy GB7 and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
